WEBVTT

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.470
<i>Arashi...</i>

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.600
<i>Arashi...</i>

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.060
<i>I may never see him again.</i>

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:25.150
<i>I had totally forgotten.
That's the kind of world this is.</i>

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:28.270
<i>This is the kind of place we're in.</i>

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.070
It's going to be okay, Nat.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.150
I'm sure he's just fine.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.320
Matsuri...

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.410
That's Arashi's kite.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:45.120
If we fly this kite, he'll see it
and be sure to come back.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.380
And if he doesn't see it,
then that just means he's unlucky.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.380
Semmy!

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:56.590
<i>Semimaru is just doing what he can
for Arashi, in the only way he knows how.</i>

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:04.480
Hey! Something weird is happening!

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.940
The surface of the ocean
has turned totally green.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.690
What is this? Algae?

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.200
The current has stopped.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.410
Hey, Ryo.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.620
There's something out there.

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.040
They're ships! There's a ton of them!

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.590
Ryo? Is something wrong?

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.340
No. It's nothing.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.720
<i>I have to keep my eyes on Ango and Ryo.</i>

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.140
<i>These teenagers have their own guns.</i>

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.100
<i>How come?</i>

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.150
WHITE DEW

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:18.280
-Ango.
-I know, this is bad.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.950
Natsu, get one of the spare ropes.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:21.950
Oh, sure.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:26.410
What are you going to do?

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.790
We're going to tow the ship
with this boat.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.250
We have to get away from here.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.960
You don't have to do that.
It'll move again eventually.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.960
-Or it may not ever again.
-What?

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.960
Based on the number of
abandoned ships around here,

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:43.760
it's possible that there's no current
in this area for some reason.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.430
The fact that there's so much algae here
means it's unable to flow anywhere else.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:53.900
If we're not careful,
we could get stuck here forever.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.520
It's so heavy!

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.730
And it reeks!

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.190
It's like liquid concrete!
We cannot row through this!

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:02.860
Shut up and row.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.030
You know, this algae--

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:06.120
Don't touch it!

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:09.160
Just have a look.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.410
It's incredibly sticky!

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.410
It stuck fast to the boat in no time.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.620
We'll never move no matter what we try.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.920
There's no way we can move this ship.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:30.560
<i>I can get liquids this way
and warm up as well.</i>

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.690
<i>I wonder if these barnacle things are
edible too.</i>

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:44.030
What?

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.910
It's a windmill.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.760
That's my kite! The ship must be below it!

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:13.350
This ship isn't even budging
a single inch.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:18.020
<i>I want to look for Arashi,
but we're totally stuck here.</i>

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.940
<i>What can I possibly do?</i>

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:24.860
Semimaru, what are you doing?

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.200
I think there might be something
on those old ships over there.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.740
You know, like canned food and stuff.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.240
I think I can reach them
using this ladder.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.830
Wow! That sounds fun! I'll go with you!

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.040
Want to come, Nat?

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.830
What? Me?

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.790
No.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.000
Hey, that's dangerous.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.710
I'm just going for a quick look.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:44.710
I won't go too far.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.550
Just leave him be, Ango.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.260
<i>These people...</i>

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.470
<i>They're so careless,
yet somehow they're still alive.</i>

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.430
Gross!

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.060
It's no good. The wood is all mush.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:58.810
I'm surprised it hasn't sunk.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.060
Oh, it must be thanks to the algae.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.360
-What a catch!
-What a catch!

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.280
The underside of the deck is
covered in shellfish!

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:13.450
Crabs too!

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.290
For now, let's have a feast!

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.460
Too bad we can't eat algae.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.920
Now's not the time for this.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.040
They're ready!

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.420
Smells great!

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.380
<i>I'm surprised that they can have
so much fun at a time like this.</i>

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:31.680
<i>The old me would have wondered
why they weren't worried about Arashi.</i>

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:32.930
Here's some for you, Nat.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.510
Thank you.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.560
Cheer up.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:38.350
<i>But now, I understand.</i>

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.650
<i>Everyone is actually worried.</i>

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:44.190
<i>Which is why they're trying to do
everything they can.</i>

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.650
<i>For example, Matsuri and Semimaru,</i>

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:53.070
<i>they're thinking for themselves
and going right into action.</i>

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.290
<i>Why can't I be more like that?</i>

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:01.540
<i>What can I do to become
a more useful person?</i>

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.750
The sun has come out again.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:08.880
Now that you mention it,
the fog is breaking up.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.300
What the?

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.310
What is that?

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:18.600
A wall? A building? A ship?

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:19.980
It's huge!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.440
A tanker? Wait... An aircraft carrier?

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.030
Ryo?

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:34.160
<i>We could still be in that test.</i>

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:38.450
<i>They might still be testing us.</i>

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.290
-There's a picture on it.
-What?

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:45.380
There, on the hull. It's a little faded.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.750
You're right. What is that?

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.090
An elephant?

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:52.180
The god Śakra riding on a white elephant?

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.590
No, wait. That's Samantabhadra.

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:57.510
A Buddhist image?
Then this is one of the storage shelters!

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:59.220
This must be one of the seven Fujis.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:01.770
I was never told about a ship like this.

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.850
What Fuji could this be, anyway?

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:06.020
It's not one of the seven.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:07.690
What do you mean, Chimaki?

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:11.780
Directions are usually split up
into four or eight, right?

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:13.360
Seven doesn’t make sense.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:16.620
<i>When you look at the seven Fujis</i>

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:20.040
<i>marked with a Buddhist statue
that Ms. Botan mentioned,</i>

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.370
<i>the one in the southeast is missing.</i>

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:27.500
<i>The missing one is that one,
the guardian of the southeast,</i>

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:28.840
<i>Samantabhadra.</i>

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.470
If that ship is
one of the storage shelters,

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.550
then why wasn't Ms. Botan told about it?

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.180
Samantabhadra.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:42.850
He's known for showing up unexpectedly
and administering charity.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:48.730
He is a bodhisattva of reason,
and was believed to give long life.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:50.780
There must be a reason it's here.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:54.450
Say, Chimaki, how come
you know so much about this?

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:55.860
Are you a Buddhist?

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.870
I don't know any of the religious stuff.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.540
I've only studied it as a piece of art.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.000
What was Team Summer A told about
the seven Fujis?

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.210
We hadn't heard a thing.

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.630
We have no idea what all this is.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.800
Perhaps it's different for each team.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.590
Anyway, it doesn't really matter.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.380
There's no wind,

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:19.180
the ship is stuck in stinky concrete algae
so we can't even look for Arashi,

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:23.220
so there's nothing else for us to do
but check out that ship, right?

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.310
We might find something we can use.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.480
I agree!

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.650
It's so huge, it must be packed
to the brim full of goodies.

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:33.610
The only problem is figuring out
how we'll get over there.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.660
There is a way over,
but it would be stupid to go.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:38.740
Leave them be.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:42.490
<i>If you can sense trouble in the air,
there's no need to go.</i>

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.620
<i>In fact, you mustn't go.</i>

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:45.870
Oh, I know!

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:51.460
And then hop on!

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.500
I knew it! It won't sink!

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:57.510
If we connect a bunch of these together,
we can walk over to that ship!

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.260
Hey, Teacher, there aren't enough doors.

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.510
Which is why...

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:04.770
After you get on the next one,

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:08.100
you pick up the door you were on before...

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:10.020
and put it down next.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.860
If we just keep repeating this,
we'll be just fine.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.400
Am I a genius or what?

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:16.820
That'll take forever.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:18.650
Semimaru is amazing.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:22.240
Well, that's about the only way to do it.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.830
I'm surprised that dummy figured it out.

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:26.750
Okay!

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:38.050
I see a ladder that looks like
it goes up to the deck.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:40.180
We might be able to get inside.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:43.260
Big Sis! Matsuri! Follow me!

00:10:43.970 --> 00:10:45.220
What about you two?

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:46.850
We'd never risk it.

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.810
Excuse me...

00:10:50.190 --> 00:10:52.480
Would it be okay if I came too?

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.020
You really want to come, Nat?

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:59.450
Yes. If you need something carried,
I think I can do that.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:06.830
<i>I have to do my best
and find a way to be useful.</i>

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.580
<i>Everyone else is trying hard,
so I should too.</i>

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:16.750
Don't do it, Natsu.
There's no reason to walk into danger.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.220
Oh, Ango's making a move!

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:20.220
But...

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:24.510
if Semimaru and Matsuri are going,
then I think I should join them.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:32.400
<i>Back then, if I had stayed with him,
then Shigeru wouldn't have died.</i>

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:35.940
Then I'm going too.

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.070
What?

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.610
Ango...

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:39.900
Get ready.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:44.530
I think he likes you, Nat!

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.910
What's your next move?

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.830
I really doubt that.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.960
But I can tell that he's worried about me.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:53.710
How about you, Ryo? Will you come too?

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.290
Come on, it'll be like going on a picnic.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:57.880
No, thanks.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:02.840
What's wrong, Hotaru?

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:04.800
Why are you looking at my hand?

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:08.680
It's nothing, please don't mind me.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:12.810
Ms. Botan, I'll come with you
and the others.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:14.560
I'm really curious.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:16.810
I'll stay here.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:19.020
Okay, then get ready.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.440
Bring drinking water.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:26.700
I can't believe how stupid you are.
It's pissing me off.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.030
Ryo...

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:32.250
This is obviously a test for them.

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.960
This won't end well.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:39.420
You might even end up contaminated
by a virus like at that shelter out west.

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:41.300
Ryo.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:44.050
It's my fault that Shigeru died.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.050
If only I had my act together.

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:52.930
Back then, I hurt my leg.
And this time, it's my hand.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:54.520
I was so pathetic!

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:57.860
But I got my act together now!
I can do more than before!

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.400
I can save Shigeru!

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.730
How is your hand doing?

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:06.360
You should probably start moving it
and start physical therapy.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:10.280
I thought so too,
but I still can't move two fingers.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:13.750
They don't hurt when I touch them,
so I think they've healed.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.330
Were the nerves cut?

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:18.580
If only Ban were here.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:22.550
If Nijiko were here,
she definitely wouldn't go.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:27.300
Ango, take your gun with you.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:28.300
Ryo...

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:32.390
Who knows what we'll run into.
You can use it with your left hand, right?

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:34.810
No problem.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:38.400
Okay, let's give this our best shot!

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.400
Be careful, Nat.

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:47.030
What? You're going with them, Ryo?

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:51.030
Yes, even though I've run into trouble
like this twice before.

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.660
What happens twice
will surely happen a third time.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:56.540
I guess this means
you must like this sort of thing.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:01.340
I'm not that type at all,
so a part of me is jealous.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.840
I like this sort of thing?

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:07.220
You piss me off sometimes.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:13.060
You're coming with us, Ryo? Hooray!

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:14.350
Let's go!

00:14:15.470 --> 00:14:16.810
By the way, Chimaki,

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.770
make sure to take down the sails later.

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:20.770
How do I do that?

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:23.440
All you have to do is
pull on that rope really hard.

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:26.280
I know you'll be alone here,
so be careful.

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:30.160
Okay, you too.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:50.010
How far will they go?

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:52.390
<i>I'll survive by myself...</i>

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.720
<i>until I find Arashi.</i>

00:14:57.310 --> 00:15:00.350
What? You came with me? Are you okay?

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.480
I'm not even sure we'll find water.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.410
<i>This world is just so beautiful.</i>

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:35.430
Incredible. It's a forest!

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.690
The air is suddenly so much cooler.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:50.280
Water! All right!

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.160
What a strange shape.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:58.790
That's for sure.

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:01.910
I don't know much about ships, but look.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:04.290
There's something like a ladder
that goes up to the top.

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:08.380
Wait. We need to find a place to secure
a rope to keep us safe--

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.130
-I'm heading up.
-Hey!

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.300
Earlier, I climbed up a little.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:15.890
It's perfectly sturdy.
There's nothing to worry about.

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:24.190
For some reason, this thing isn't
all busted up like the others.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:25.230
It seems tougher.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:28.650
The stuff inside must still be
in good condition too.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:30.780
Let's look for an entrance.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.870
I know what this is!
It's a water cannon that shoots water.

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.580
A water cannon that shoots water?

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.960
You think that's redundant, don't you?

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:47.170
I didn't say that!

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.130
I was thinking the same thing!
It's like saying,

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:51.420
-"falling down from a horse."
-Semimaru! Cut it out.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:52.630
Semimaru!

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:56.050
If we sense even the slightest danger,
we're going right back.

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:00.970
Natsu, don't get separated.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:03.140
Oh, right.

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:11.280
What? It opened.

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:14.650
Hey, Ryo. Isn't this one of those...

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:17.030
solar power systems?

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:19.700
Maybe.

00:17:21.870 --> 00:17:24.910
This was made in a very odd manner.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:30.000
Hotaru, what were you thinking
when you looked at my hand earlier?

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:32.170
I caught a glimpse of your fortune.

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:33.630
And?

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.010
It made me a little curious.

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:37.840
Is it okay if I tell you?

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:39.510
So what is it?

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.890
You are keeping a secret.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:43.930
You are debating
as to whether to share it.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.770
But a time will come
when you will share it naturally.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:49.020
What does that mean?

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:50.520
I don't know.

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:52.570
That's just the impression I got.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.860
Hotaru, we found an entrance.
Come with me.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:56.780
Okay.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:06.790
What exactly is this smell?

00:18:07.410 --> 00:18:08.580
<i>Is it rust?</i>

00:18:10.670 --> 00:18:13.550
Lights! The lights came on! No way!

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.670
This place still has power!

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:19.090
It must be able to detect humans.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.850
Or maybe there are people here.

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:24.600
I bet there might be survivors.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:31.690
Let's go and find out.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.370
No way!

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.910
It's not all of them,
but some of them are turning.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:51.580
<i>I'll follow the cables.</i>

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.750
<i>They're in the same direction as the kite.</i>

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:06.930
Oh, I forgot.
I need to take down the sails.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:15.440
So I just pull on this rope
really hard, right?

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:36.000
<i>I... can't move.</i>

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:44.300
Is this the cockpit?

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:47.220
What would you call that on a ship?

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:49.890
What is this?

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:53.900
Don't touch anything!

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.520
Are any of these machines working?

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:01.400
PROCESSING

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:05.160
This one says
that it's processing something.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:07.910
I bet it was off but got turned on again.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:11.910
Right, except there doesn't seem
to be any signs of survivors.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:16.000
For now,
let's take a look around this floor.

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:20.420
Nobody goes downstairs just yet.

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:26.180
If only we could find a record
or journal of some sort.

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:35.400
<i>There it is again.</i>

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:39.320
<i>What is it? It looks like something
from a limestone cave.</i>

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:42.530
<i>Maybe it's just rusted over.</i>

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:45.450
What?

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:47.700
Hey, Ryo, aren't you going inside?

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:53.160
Don't you like ships or something, Ryo?

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:57.580
When we found all the wrecked ships
and even when we saw this one,

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.420
you looked pretty unhappy.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.430
Your group, Summer B,
you're always watching people, aren't you?

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:08.180
That's one of the basics
of getting along with others.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:10.600
It's listing.

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.230
<i>The stern is sinking!</i>

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:19.230
The door just closed!

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:21.440
<i>This ship is...</i>

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:22.690
<i>...at this time.</i>

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:27.530
<i>All doors and passageways
will be temporarily sealed.</i>

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:28.660
<i>All passengers...</i>

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:32.370
<i>...in your assigned positions
until completion.</i>

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:33.370
"Completion"?

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:34.870
<i>Due to the risk of danger...</i>

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:37.210
<i>...advised to refrain</i>

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.590
-<i>from all unnecessary movements.</i>
-What's going on? Is someone here?

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:52.470
No!

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:54.640
I'm going to fall!

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:03.530
Natsu!

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:15.660
That ship just...
